  "/theorems/028ccdb8-1f42-4651-94d3-63758b6500fd": {
    "data": {
      "audits": [],
      "created_at": "2026-09-30T06:26:41.254192+00:00",
      "deprecated_at": null,
      "deprecated_by": null,
      "formal_statement": "namespace CookPvsNP\n\n/-- Polynomial-time computable functions are closed under composition. -/\ntheorem polyTimeComputable_comp {Sym\u2081 Sym\u2082 Sym\u2083 : Type}\n    (f : List Sym\u2081 \u2192 List Sym\u2082) (g : List Sym\u2082 \u2192 List Sym\u2083)\n    (hf : PolyTimeComputable f) (hg : PolyTimeComputable g) :\n    PolyTimeComputable (g \u2218 f) := by\n  sorry\n\nend CookPvsNP",
      "mathlib_rev": "0df444a360eaa60ab8c11dca51a86af692955474",
      "natural_language_statement": "Cook's polynomial-time many-one reducibility (Definition 3, p. 2) compares languages by means of polynomial-time computable functions. This is the closure of that function class under composition: if f is polynomial-time computable from \u03a3\u2081* to \u03a3\u2082* and g is polynomial-time computable from \u03a3\u2082* to \u03a3\u2083*, then g after f is polynomial-time computable as well. It is exactly what makes reducibility itself transitive, and hence what allows an NP-hardness argument to be assembled as a chain of separate reductions instead of one monolithic function. The proof is the standard simulation of the first machine followed by the second, on one tape, with the polynomial time bounds composed.",
      "preamble": "import Mathlib\nimport Definitions.Def_CookPvsNP_defs",
      "readback": null,
      "source": "Cook, The P versus NP problem, Clay Mathematics Institute (2000), \u00a71 p. 2 and Definition 3 p. 2",
      "status": "Open",
      "tags": [
        "complexity-theory",
        "np-hardness",
        "source-faithful-child"
      ],
      "theorem_id": "028ccdb8-1f42-4651-94d3-63758b6500fd",
      "theorem_name": "CookPvsNP.polyTimeComputable_comp",
      "theorem_title": "Cook, Definition 3 \u2014 polynomial-time computable functions are closed under composition",
      "visibility": "public",
      "vote_count": 0
    },
    "ok": true
